----- SOURCE CODE

pub type Wibble {
  Wibble(a: Int, b: Int)
  Wobble(a: Int, c: Int)
}

pub fn main(wibble) {
  case wibble {
    Wibble(..) -> Wibble(..wibble, b: 10)
    Wobble(..) -> panic
  }
}


----- WARNING
warning: Incompatible i version range
  ┌─ /src/warning/wrn.i:9:28
  │
9 │     Wibble(..) -> Wibble(..wibble, b: 10)
  │                            ^^^^^^ This requires an i version >= 0.1.0

Record updates for custom types when the variant is known was introduced in
version v0.1.0. But the i version range specified in your `i.toml` would
allow this code to run on an earlier version like v0.0.1, resulting in
compilation errors!

Hint: Remove the version constraint from your `i.toml` or update it to be:

    i = ">= 0.1.0"
